  "proof_chain": [
    "Set e=epsilon/3 and use the existing all-depth radial error theorem to choose one h with 0<h<=1/8 before N.",
    "Intersect its eventual bound with the existing all-depth noncoprime bound, the existing all-depth proper-cell bound at the same e, and N>=2.",
    "After selecting N in that intersection, quantify over every allowed t and every original dependent B dep p; instantiate the noncoprime and proper bounds at the same selected h.",
    "Rewrite allDepthSelectedProperStripMass through its exact existing cell dictionary to match the proper supplier's raw Fin431/cell/p/l/s target.",
    "Use N>=2 to obtain nonnegative norm and multiply the exact actual all-depth inner comparison without changing the original sharp coefficient.",
    "Apply the existing full profile=inner+outer identity, keep the original marked ordinaryBad sum literally, and add the three full-depth epsilon/3 allowances."
  ],
